	(text "UART/SBUS Jumper\n\nBy default the RC input is configured for SBUS \n(inverted) protocol. To use a radio that uses a\n normal (noninverted) UART signal, cut the trace\n between the SBUS and center solder pad and solder \nthe jumper on the back of the Navigator PCB to the\n UART position. To reconfigure the RC input for \nSBUS after the trace has been cut, solder the \njumper in the SBUS position."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
